   "line": [
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The move is the pawn to d5 — declining the gambit outright. It's exceedingly rare, and precisely because of that, if White isn't accurate he can end up slightly worse. This is the whole point: a practical weapon that dodges the booked-up main lines.",
   "kind": "trap",
   "teaches": "3...d5 declines the Morra and returns the initiative — surprise value plus soundness.",
   "plans": "...d5, take over if White drifts."
